{
  "$comment": [
    "Rocket audio spec — the SOURCE of the game's music and sound effects.",
    "",
    "Read by `scripts/rocket/generate-audio.js`, which RENDERS these patterns to",
    "WAV files in `frontend/public/rocket/audio/` plus a `manifest.json` the game",
    "reads at runtime. Deterministic, offline, no accounts and no per-second cost.",
    "",
    "Why patterns rather than prompts: this game's art is flat retro cartoon, so a",
    "chiptune score fits it better than generic AI music, and nothing here depends",
    "on a paid subscription. Each item also carries a `prompt` describing the intent",
    "in words — that is what an AI provider (ElevenLabs, Suno, ...) would be given if",
    "one is ever wired up, and it documents what the track is meant to feel like.",
    "",
    "Pattern notation, one string per bar:",
    "  note      C4 D#3 Eb2 F#5   (letters, optional #/b, octave)",
    "  rest      .",
    "  hold      -            extends the previous note by one step",
    "  drum hit  x",
    "Steps default to 16 per bar (4 beats x 4 sixteenths). A track's phrase cycles",
    "until `bars` are filled, so a 2-bar phrase repeated 4x is written once.",
    "",
    "Cost/size knob: `output.sampleRate`. 22050 Hz mono ~= 44 KB per second of audio",
    "(so the whole set is ~2 MB, comparable to the sprite set). 44100 doubles it and",
    "crisps up the hats."
  ],

  "output": {
    "dir": "frontend/public/rocket/audio",
    "format": "wav",
    "sampleRate": 22050,
    "channels": 1,
    "peak": 0.89
  },

  "defaults": {
    "tempo": 120,
    "bars": 8,
    "beatsPerBar": 4,
    "stepsPerBeat": 4
  },

  "instruments": {
    "pad": {
      "wave": "saw",
      "detune": 7,
      "gain": 0.15,
